"――Yes, I kept it concealed. It was by my own judgment."

Faced with a head-on confrontation, Russell showed no significant sign of agitation; if anything, it was Subaru, the one pressing for answers, who ended up getting thrown off balance.

Having received consecutive declarations of resolve from Melty and 'Black Dog', he had just confirmed with Russell the grave truth revealed therein—Emilia and the others' escape from the royal castle.

"For now, the castle is on standby above the clouds. Combining its ascent to the altitude limit with the effects of the 'Cognitive Disruption Cloak', we should be able to buy some time. During that window, we shall determine our next move and general policy. Does that suit you?"

So went the judgment of Russell, who had released his hands from the black sphere used to pilot the castle—the 'Heaven Control Sphere'—bringing Kugelschreiber Castle to a dead halt in the middle of the sky. As a side note, Subaru had pushed for the name 'Ball Steering Wheel', but it should be added that Beatrice had shot it down on the grounds that it already had an official name.

"Betty would like to take Subaru's side, but one cannot simply ignore a name Mother bestowed first, in fact. Betty will tell you all sorts of things about this castle later, I suppose."

"That's a promise, then. Come to think of it, retrieving that thing you left behind kind of got swept under the rug too."

To begin with, before the 'Beloved Children' attacked, Subaru and the others had been on their way to retrieve something Beatrice had left behind in the castle four hundred years ago. That gift from her mother would need to be properly returned to Beatrice's hands as well.

To that end—,

"I was hoping we could clear the air and completely sort out our bad blood right here, but..."

"I agree. While harboring hidden motives, it is not easy to open one's heart to another. I, too, constantly wish this were a world where everyone could show their hands."

"Except for yourself... is that it, in fact? Wanting to always hold a trump card no one else possesses sounds just like Roswaal's friend, I suppose."

"Hmm, while I understand he is someone close to you, I must call it a bad habit to bring up Roswaal to evaluate me at every turn. 'Librarian', you may fail to see the true essence of things that way."

"W-W-What in the world, in fact...!"

Called out on it, Beatrice looked back on her own words and froze in horror.

Subaru had assumed she was doing it deliberately, but it seemed it was entirely unconscious. Patting Beatrice's head as she froze in place, having realized she had constantly been keeping the absent Roswaal in mind, Subaru sharpened his voice: "Russell-san."

"――'Silver Fox', please. Even if no one else is around, you should not let your guard down."

"My bad. But as far as this goes, part of me is doing it on purpose. Isn't it about time we spoke frankly with each other? Melty-chan and 'Black Dog' did that for us."

"And you come to negotiate directly on behalf of those two?"

"I heard that storming up to their boss is a life-or-death gamble. It's not like I'm being used by them or anything."

"I see, wise indeed. ――However, the curse marks on 'White Sheep' and 'Black Dog' were engraved with both parties fully aware of the risks. It would be unreasonable to lodge complaints after the fact."

"Even if someone could stomach being kept from revealing secrets, sealing off objections entirely is going way too far. Whether it's a dictator or a one-man corporate tyrant, if the person at the top screws up at the helm, it's game over... If the fate of a nation is what's on the line, you could stand to be a lot more cautious."

"Cautious, you say? ――I fully intend to be just that, more than anyone."

Slightly lowering his tone, Russell slowly shook his head.

Catching a complex shade of emotion laced within that murmur, Subaru felt a snag and knitted his brows. But before he could give shape to that snag, Russell met his eyes.

"Those two... 'White Sheep' and 'Black Dog' lean inherently toward good. I could easily imagine that spending a long time together would lead to them opening up to you. And that, in turn, would lead to you taking their side as well. It comes as no surprise."

"Then is it that Russell-san can't get along with us because you think of yourself as leaning toward the villains?"

"No, I do not perceive myself as a villain. ――If pressed to say, I am nothingness."

"...Nothingness?"

As Subaru reflexively asked back, Russell silently pulled his chin back and cast his eyes across the room.

The place where Subaru and the others were currently speaking with Russell was the laboratory of the 'Witch' Echidna, who had been the master of Kugelschreiber Castle—a room where they had returned the documents they had once tried to carry out, deciding to spend time browsing and scrutinizing them anew.

It was eerie, but since the proper guest rooms were already being used by Crusch and Ferris, the reason for this choice of venue was simply that no other room came to mind that was suitable for a private conversation.

Gazing emotionlessly around such a room, Russell continued without meeting their eyes.

"Originally, fearing the possibility that a bird-letter might not arrive, multiple were sent out. The one who brought you that confidential report was likely 'Black Dog'. That was an action skating extremely close to violating the agreements of the curse mark, but... in the first place, those two are not in a position where they swore loyalty to the Kingdom. A slight slip-through is well within expectations."

"Since you've already figured it out, I'll just say it: 'Black Dog' said he peeked at the bird-letter. ...If it's an important report, doesn't sending out a bunch of them just increase the risk accordingly?"

"There are conditions for opening a bird-letter. To open a bird-letter of the 'Six Tongues', one must have the identical curse mark engraved upon them. It is a condition that even the 'Beloved Children' cannot satisfy."

"...A curse mark is a pledge that binds the soul of the recipient, I suppose. If there are unique rules to the curse mark of the 'Six Tongues', imitating it is nearly impossible, in fact. It makes for optimal security, I suppose."

To Russell's reply to Subaru's concern, Beatrice added that supplement.

Giving a firm hug to Beatrice, who had somehow managed to pull her heart together from the Roswaal-shock, Subaru understood how 'Black Dog' had been able to intercept the bird-letter.

Still, just as Russell said, it must have been cutting it awfully close.

"By the way, what if it hadn't just cut it close, but gone completely over the line?"

"One would be tormented by unbearable agony throughout their entire body. If one were to leak a secret that must not be revealed, even their life would be no exception. Following these rules... regulations, we have held our own against the 'Beloved Children'."

"And because you're completely steeped in that, Russell-san, you aren't shaken no matter what happens to anyone? Is that why you call yourself nothingness? But a human heart isn't that simple."

That was right. A person's heart wasn't some convenient tool that would never crack just because one decided it was so.

Even those who possessed values incomprehensible to ordinary people, like the Sin Archbishops and the 'Witches', should never be able to escape being bound by the thing known as their own heart.

And yet—,

"If the world one sees is different, what is shaped upon it changes as well. Humans have human reason, spirits have spirit reason, and beasts have beast reason. None of those apply to me. I am an inhuman being, neither spirit nor beast... No, a slave to the system."

"A slave... to the system, you say?"

"I do not seek empathy. Nor do I seek understanding. When two paths are weighed and compared within me, the one of higher value is chosen. That is an absolute guiding principle within me."

"...Is that your excuse for hiding what was going on with Emilia and the others?"

"It is a disclosure of my judgment criteria. You are free to deem it an excuse or a cover-up, however."

Subaru perceived that a deep, massive line had been drawn.

He did not think Russell was trying to baffle them with intangible, incomprehensible logic. Russell was likely engaging with them with his own brand of sincerity. It was just that, as he himself acknowledged, his criteria for judgment were vastly different from Subaru's.

A person's standing and circumstances played a large part in shaping how they were. But more than his position as director of the 'Six Tongues', the foremost factor defining Russell's very existence was likely the 'Divine Protection of Evaluation'.

'—They say that the famed "Hoshin of the Wilderness" possessed the same Divine Protection as well, you know.'

That was a topic that had briefly come up in a casual chat with Russell before.

Hearing that, Subaru's feelings had been quite complex—the reason being that Subaru had presumed the figure named Hoshin, who founded the Kararagi City-States, was someone who had been summoned from another world just like himself. But with Hoshin being a 'Divine Protection holder', that theory became considerably suspect.

If it were a pattern like Subaru's, where an Authority sprouted after the fact, or if it wasn't a summoning to another world, but rather an outright reincarnation, the story would change—though that theorizing could wait for later.

The role played by that 'Hoshin of the Wilderness', who possessed the 'Divine Protection of Evaluation', had been immense—a monstrous feat passed down across hundreds of years.

A person capable of accomplishing such a feat naturally possessed an eye and values distinct from others, and the same could be said for Russell. For that reason, he did not seek understanding.

Because—,

"Whether to seek understanding or not is something you've already compared and reached an answer on, too."

"――Yes. That is precisely it."

To Subaru's shuddering remark, Russell softened his lips and nodded.

That pleasant smile, free of sarcasm or offense, actually inspired a feeling bordering on awe at the sheer harshness of the road Russell had walked, when one considered that the process that shaped it was so different from other people's.

So to speak, it was like mingling among a crowd of aliens whose ways of seeing and feeling the world differed from one's own, spending one's days making sure they never found out you were different from those around you.

If he had relied on his Divine Protection to judge even the success or failure of that—,

"Please do not expect change. This is who I am. That will not waver."

"――――"

"――. Not even spirits can remain unchanging. Your way of thinking is far too biased, in fact."

Hearing Russell's conclusion, Beatrice, having lived for an immense span of time, stated with a bitter face.

Beatrice's argument, however, held meaning only because Beatrice was someone with the will to change; the reality was that it did not resonate with Russell, who could find no value in it.

Feeling that divide acutely, Subaru exhaled a long breath.

"I get why you kept it quiet. And that there's no point poking at you about why. So at least tell me the details. You've got them, right? Something more detailed and more up to date than what 'Black Dog' had."

"Do you not consider that having concealed information once, I might falsify it next?"

"I do. I do, so just give it up already. From here on, it's a matter of trust. And speaking on that trust, I don't buy the story that you don't know what happened to Emilia and the others afterward."

"Hmm, may I ask the reason?"

"The 'Six Tongues' have already lost track of my companions once before. Character-wise, Russell-san, you're not the type to make the same mistake twice. What's more, the castle's vigilance should have been at the absolute maximum of maximums."

If the 'Six Tongues' had been founded to protect the Kingdom of Lugunica, the safety of royal selection candidates like Emilia should have been one of their supreme priorities. At the very least, they wouldn't have adopted a policy of disregarding them. Surveillance should have been directed toward them to a degree well beyond ordinary.

Under Subaru's intense gaze, Russell fell silent for a moment before beginning to speak.

That was—,

"――Lady Emilia and Lady Felt, who were placed under house arrest in the royal castle, escaped the castle under the guidance of Captain Marcos Gildark of the Royal Guard, and are currently on the run. For some reason, it appears that Lady Filore, the new royal selection candidate, is accompanying them, however."

"――! That scary-faced Captain got Emilia and the others out? And Filore is with them too... Are they... going to be okay?"

Presented with unexpected circumstances, Subaru's eyes went wide in rigid shock.

Marcos, who was said to have taken Emilia and the others out, was the Captain of the Royal Guard—meaning he was Reinhard and Julius's superior, a figure occupying a vital position in the Kingdom. For such a man to defy the orders of the royal castle and flee with royal selection candidates, turmoil in the Royal Capital was inevitable.

On top of that, with Filore also being there—,

"Melty-chan seems to judge that Filore is in the clear even within the 'Divine Dragon Church', and I don't think that girl is capable of scheming anything, but..."

"It appears she joined this not as the Saintess of the 'Divine Dragon Church', but as a private individual. That said, her primary knight is accompanying her, it seems."

"Filore's primary knight, meaning..."

"――As you know, Heinkel Astrea."

That, too, was a fact made known during the two months since Filore had become a royal selection candidate, and had been one of the fairly shocking topics surrounding the royal selection.

Within Subaru, an impression of the man named Heinkel was quite difficult to settle on. While it was true his first impression had been the absolute worst, between his actions in the Vollachia Empire and the suspicion of him siding with Al while Subaru and Beatrice had been sealed inside the black orb, he was a man extraordinarily hard to evaluate.

Still, Subaru had felt that Heinkel ingratiating himself with Filore and using that good-natured girl to his advantage—was perhaps not quite what was happening.

"Even so, that's just a gut feeling mixed with wishful thinking. Emilia-tan and Felt are probably gonna feel crazy awkward around that old guy, too."

"If you mean a lack of lively conversation, the Captain of the Royal Guard is a strong contender as well, I suppose. ...Even knowing the detailed circumstances, one cannot stop worrying, in fact."

"Marcos-san is strong, sure, but..."

Having actually clashed with the 'Beloved Children', he knew that their trickiness lay not in simple combat capability, but in the wickedness of their foul play utilizing their strange abilities. And according to one consideration Natsuki Subaru had reached in his life in another world, the combat powerhouses of this world were weak to foul play.

Because for them, battle was something where the one who hit harder first often won.

Therefore, Subaru considered his role to be seeing through the opponent's foul play, and on top of that, deploying his companions appropriately into positions where they could hit the opponent harder first.

"Deploying the winning hand in a place where it can win. It's like making them play a game of rock-paper-scissors they can't lose. For that, we really need to reunite with Emilia-tan and the others—"

"――If you intend to defect to rendezvous with them, I shall activate the curse marks of 'White Sheep' and 'Black Dog'."

"Huh?"

His complexion changing, evenly divided between an anxious heart and an impatient one, Subaru could not wrap his head around Russell's continued words for an instant.

What had Russell just said? ――Activate Melty's and 'Black Dog's' curse marks?

"...Betty does not understand the meaning, I suppose. Even if you kill those two, there is no benefit in it for you, in fact."

"I do not recall saying I would take their lives. Activating the curse marks... as I mentioned earlier, merely inflicts unbearable agony. It is a torment as if one's soul were being torn apart; something one would never wish to taste a second time."

"The way you say that makes it sound as though you, too..."

"I have. Do you think I have been in my current position since the day I was born? There was a time when I, too, was like 'White Sheep' and the others... in a position to receive, rather than bestow. That is why I know. Just how much agony it entails."

"――――"

As Russell spoke flatly in a tone that brooked no doubt of falsehood, cold sweat ran down Subaru's cheek.

It was an unmistakable threat, but it was obvious it wasn't mere lip service. Russell possessed an inhuman quality that instilled certainty that he would carry it out. To borrow Beatrice's words, that was just what one would expect from Roswaal's best friend.

And—,

"...Betty's answer is the same as before, I suppose. Even if you torment the two instead of killing them, that is meaningless to Betty and Subaru, in fact."

"――Do you truly think so, 'Librarian'?"

At that inquiry, Beatrice beside Subaru shuddered in the shoulders. Beatrice's gaze flickered to Subaru standing beside her, biting her lip in frustration.

He tried his best not to let it show on his face. But as expected, it was impossible. It showed. ――That Russell's threat was overwhelmingly effective against Subaru.

"I believe I told you. It was easy to imagine those two would open up to you."

"Then the reason you didn't make that threat earlier was..."

"Because it is a threat that would not display its maximum effect until you... strictly speaking, until 'Gray Star' developed an attachment to those two."

"You really are Roswaal's friend, I suppose."

"For now, I shall meekly swallow that assessment."

To Beatrice, who spat the words out bitterly, Russell did not so much as twitch a facial muscle.

Yet, in truth, his intentions had all but succeeded. Knowing that Melty and the others would be made to taste torture-like agony because he made a move, Subaru could not choose that.

However, resting on the other side of the scale was none other than Emilia herself.

"Russell-san...!"

"I will not say something like 'this was a measure I did not wish to take'. If necessary, I flip the necessary cards. My judgment criteria are as I told you."

"...A curse mark is something bound to the soul. Seeing as it requires the consent of the party involved to engrave, undoing it from the outside is an impossible feat, in fact."

To Subaru's teeth-gritting glare, Russell's reply was cold, and Beatrice gave an answer preempting the move Subaru would likely wish for next.

Undoing the curse mark was impossible, and Russell's values, just like his way of being, could not be changed either. ――Even so, when it came to the impossible and the unchangeable, the same went for Subaru.

Changing Natsuki Subaru into a human being who could give up on what was precious to him was utterly impossible.

Therefore—,

"――――"

Think. Think until his thoughts burned into him, until his brain cells reached a boil.

In the recent battle against the 'Beloved Children', he had forced a burden onto Crusch, Ferris, Melty, and 'Black Dog', while Subaru had done nothing other than almost dying. Right here, make up for the time spent lying around unable to do a thing, for the foolishness of remaining oblivious to the predicament of Emilia and the others.

After all—,

"――Take away petty smarts and cunning, and what the hell do I have left?"

Subaru squeezed Beatrice's hand tightly, and with his other hand, grasped the black orb at his chest. In both hands, what he clutched was determination and resolve—with that, he stoked the fires of his soul and faced forward.

Natsuki Subaru would not change. If Russell Fellow was the same—,

"――Beako, is there something to write with here? A brush, a pencil, a crayon, anything's fine!"

"――! A crayon is a bit beyond Betty, I suppose. But there is one, in fact!"

Seeing the profile of Subaru facing forward, Beatrice bounced her twintails and darted off. Bringing back a black, brush-like object from a small room in the back of the laboratory,

"Use this, I suppose! It is a brush Mother used to use, and the ink never runs out, in fact."

"The underlying mechanism is totally unknown and terrifying! But thanks. Next... I can use this as scrap paper, right?"

With the brush of unknown mechanism in hand, Subaru pulled a sheet from the documents stacked on the nearby workbench. It was one of the sheets Russell had appraised beforehand and judged unnecessary. After confirming there was nothing on the back of the old paper, Subaru ran the brush across it.

"――? 'Librarian', what is 'Gray Star' doing all of a sudden...?"

"Hmph, Betty does not know either, I suppose. But there is one thing Betty does know, in fact. ――Subaru is about to knock your socks off, I suppose."

"――――"

Unable to grasp Subaru's true intention, yet faced with Beatrice's attitude brimming with conviction, Russell narrowed his eyes. To live up to Beatrice's trust, he had to knock his socks off. ――Even if he couldn't knock his socks off, he just had to believe this attempt would work.

――Russell placed the magnitude, or rather the fluctuation, of value via his 'Divine Protection of Evaluation' as the primary focus of his judgment criteria.

Given that he had deduced the entrance of Kugelschreiber Castle where the 'Beloved Children' had attacked through a crash in value, and had applied it to the adoption of strategies and choices, its accuracy was likely high. That was evident from the fact that he had held his own against Capella, who was virtually the worst enemy imaginable in an intelligence war.

However, precisely because of that, Russell should not be able to lie to that Divine Protection of his.

In that case—,

"――This ought to work on you!"

Saying so, Subaru folded the paper he had hastily written across, tore the creased sheet down the middle into two, held one in each hand, and turned back to face Russell.

Then, he shoved the papers held in his left and right hands before Russell. What was written upon them was—,

"A comparison of Natsuki Subaru in the case of saving Lady Emilia, versus otherwise...?"

"That's right! This one is me if we save Emilia! High emotional stability, and high trust in Russell-san for sharing information! A me with increased combat power and plenty of moves at my disposal! And conversely, the me if we don't save her is..."

"Deep in paranoia and worry, with trust in you plunged into the negatives for being willing to use blackmail. Combat power remains stagnant and his mind is elsewhere... A Subaru with nothing going for him, in fact."

"Yeah, that!"

What was written on the divided papers in his right hand and left hand were, simply put, choices.

Depending on the decision made here, Natsuki Subaru could become either Natsuki Subaru. He had written the differences in a bit more detail on the paper, and while the phrasing was somewhat exaggerated, there were no lies.

Naturally, the policy of continuing to act with a do-or-die resolve to retrieve Emilia and the others while their safety remained unknown, hoping for results that way, might not be completely out of the question.

However, Natsuki Subaru had conviction.

He was a human being who could be stronger when he was with that precious person, rather than when he was worrying about them—.

"How about it, Russell-san? You've made it this far by trusting that Divine Protection of yours. With that 'Divine Protection of Evaluation' of yours, discern thoroughly which version of me holds more value to you, and choose your next words."

"――――"

"Do not tell a lie... No, you likely cannot do that anyway, so there is no need to worry, I suppose. At any rate, we have other matters to attend to, in fact."

Saying so, Beatrice, holding papers in both hands detailing different futures for herself just like Subaru, stepped in front of Subaru so that she aligned with Russell's field of view.

Of course, neither Subaru nor Beatrice had any proof as to which of the choices they had prepared would show 'value' in the universal sense. ――They simply believed.

And—,

"Come on, Russell-san."

"How about it, I suppose? Answer us, in fact."

"――. I, too, have spent over thirty years with these eyes of mine, but..."

"――――"

"You are only the second person. No, including 'Librarian', would that make three?"

Before Subaru and Beatrice pressing for an answer, Russell suddenly opened his mouth. Having spoken that far, he rubbed between his brows with a finger as if hesitating for a moment.

It was a gesture almost as if he were doubting the truth of what he saw with his own eyes, seeking to check them again.

"――――"

Taking plenty of time, however, Russell opened his eyelids once more and let out a short sigh. ――It seemed that what was visible to his eyes had not changed from a moment ago.

Namely—,

"The fearless fools who, using the value of what my eyes see as a reason, attempted to force me to swallow a decision that diverges vastly from my own thinking."

That was an answer attesting to which of the choices Subaru and Beatrice had presented was reflected with higher value in his eyes.

――The moment she thought she heard a tremendous roar, Emilia was already leaping down from the bed of the covered dragon carriage.

"――Keep going! Don't stop, run!"

Landing on the ground in a roll, she called out sharply to her surroundings. But she didn't know if her voice properly reached everyone. After all, the reverberating crunch of destruction was laced with tremors, violently shaking the entirety of the Milesta Dragonback Bridge.

The vibrations transmitted from the soles of her boots started deep and far away, but closed the distance all at once as if thrusting upward, finally erupting with a boom.

"――! Oh no!"

Her desperate voice was drowned out by the screams and angry shouts that rose simultaneously.

The people attempting to cross the Dragonback Bridge and the ground dragons pulling them cried out one after another, loudly voicing their confusion at the monstrous situation that had befallen them.

She understood how they felt very well. But they couldn't do that. Even if they stopped in their tracks and desperately cried for help, everyone around them was suffering from the exact same thing.

And howling shrilly with an intensity that swallowed up everyone's screams was none other than the Milesta Dragonback Bridge itself.

"No, no, no, no! This is bad, Emilia! I can't explain it well, but it's really bad!!"

Rising above the creaking screams of that bridge was Filore's tremendously loud voice.

Looking over, Filore was leaning out from the bed of the dragon carriage Emilia had leapt from, pointing behind them and flailing about with her pretty red eyes wide open.

At the same time, feeling the death throes of the violently shaking Dragonback Bridge travel right behind her—,

"――Icicle Line!"

Instantly, white chill swirled, and pale blue ice stemmed the cobblestones that were on the verge of peeling away and falling through. Spreading with the sound of cracking air, the freezing white ice caught the wheels of a dragon carriage that was about to spin out, plugging a hole that was about to swallow up an entire ground dragon.

Such emergency first aid for the bridge was at one spot, two spots, three spots—far too many to count.

"Geez! Doing something so awful just to look for us...!"

Emilia grew indignant, her long silver hair dancing as the hem of her robe fluttered in the blowing wind.

In Emilia's field of vision, upon the Dragonback Bridge where fissures of rupture were still spreading even now, more than fifty dragon carriages were traveling apart from the one Emilia and the others were riding. If one included those attempting to cross the bridge on foot, there was even the possibility that hundreds to over a thousand people were present.

To do that—,

"I won't let you! I'm reeally mad now!"

Against the pursuers who would ruthlessly claim the lives of over a thousand people without choosing their methods, Emilia took her stance, absolutely furious.

That was the curtain-raiser to the offensive and defensive battle that would mark the final day of the Milesta Dragonback Bridge—the very last time its majestic figure would ever be seen, after boasting a history of over three hundred years since its construction.
